# RailCrowd database migrations

This directory is the Alembic migration repository used by Flask-Migrate.
It is configured explicitly by `backend/app/extensions.py`, so commands can
be run from the repository root without depending on the current directory.

## Common commands

```bash
# Show the current database revision
flask --app backend.run db current

# Compare registered SQLAlchemy models with the current schema
flask --app backend.run db migrate -m "describe schema change"

# Review the generated file in backend/migrations/versions/ before applying it
flask --app backend.run db upgrade

# Show migration history
flask --app backend.run db history

# Roll back one revision (only when intentionally required)
flask --app backend.run db downgrade
```

Always inspect autogenerated migrations before upgrading. Alembic cannot infer
all data migrations or business rules. Back up persistent databases before
applying production migrations. Do not edit an already-applied migration; add
a new revision instead.

SQLite batch mode is enabled to support schema alterations that SQLite cannot
perform directly. Model modules must be imported through
`backend/app/models/__init__.py` so autogeneration can discover their metadata.
